# Entity Pattern

Entities represent domain models and business logic, separated from UI components.

## Entity Structure

Each entity should be in its own directory under `src/entities/`:
- `EntityName/EntityName.type.ts` - Zod schemas and TypeScript types
- `EntityName/useEntity.tsx` - Custom hooks for entity operations
- `EntityName/EntityName.context.tsx` - React Context for entity state (if needed)
- `EntityName/EntityName.context.provider.tsx` - Context provider component (if needed)

## Zod Schema Pattern

Always define Zod schemas and infer TypeScript types from them:

```typescript
import { z } from 'zod';

export const entityZod = z.object({
  id: z.string(),
  name: z.string(),
  email: z.email(),
  created_at: z.date(),
});

export type Entity = z.infer<typeof entityZod>;
```

## Validation

- Use Zod schemas for runtime validation
- Use `.safeParse()` for validation with error handling
- Export validation schemas for reuse in forms and API calls

## Context Pattern

When entity needs global state:
- Create context in `EntityName.context.tsx`
- Create provider in `EntityName.context.provider.tsx`
- Use ContextHole pattern to register provider in `src/app/context/context.hole.tsx`

## Examples

See `@src/entities/User/User.type.ts` for Zod schema pattern
See `@src/entities/User/auth.context.tsx` for context pattern
